Is this keepalive necessary considering we're (1) removing it from the pool, (2) cancelling the cleanup, and (3) returning a strong ref to the caller? Why not rather a simpler:

```go
func (p *WasmModulePool[T]) Get(ctx context.Context) (T, error) {
	if b, ok := p.instancePool.Get().(*pooledInstance[T]); ok {
		b.cleanup.Stop()
		return b.module, nil
	}
	return p.newInstance(ctx)
}
```
